IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-certificates-and-inspections`

-- Tests of ei4-part-vi-certificates-and-inspections.l4 (Act s 126). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the
-- subsection; none is copied from the module's output. Calendar arithmetic is done on a calendar: 30 days after 1 January is
-- 31 January; 15 days after 1 June is 16 June.

§ `s 126(1) -- certifying an unpaid amount`

-- 126(1)(b): default on 1 January 2026; the 30 days end on 31 January, so the first day for certifying is 1 February (fork F-ei4-6).
#ASSERT `s 126(1)(b) the first day on which an unpaid amount may be certified when the person is not attempting to avoid payment` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 1
-- 126(1)(a): in the Commission's opinion the person is attempting to avoid payment: certified without delay, the day after the default.
#ASSERT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part I` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2)
-- 126(1)(b): no such opinion; on 31 January the 30 days have not expired.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part I` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31)
-- 126(1)(b): on 1 February they have.
#ASSERT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part I` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)
-- 126(1): Part II and Part VII.1 amounts are covered too.
#ASSERT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part II` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part VII.1` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
-- 126(1): an amount payable under Part III or Part VII is not in the list "Part I, II or VII.1".
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part III` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part VII` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)
-- 126(1): an amount that has been paid is not an unpaid amount.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(1) the unpaid amount may be certified by the Commission` `Part I` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)

§ `s 126(2) and (3) -- judgment and costs`

-- 126(2): the registered certificate has the force of a judgment for the amount specified plus interest to the day of payment: 1000 + 25.
#ASSERT `s 126(2) the debt for which the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court` TRUE 1000 25 EQUALS JUST 1025
-- 126(2): not yet registered: the subsection says nothing. NOT COVERED: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 126(2) the debt for which the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court` FALSE 1000 25 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 126(3): reasonable costs and charges attendant on the registration are recoverable.
#ASSERT `s 126(3) the costs and charges are recoverable as if they had been certified and the certificate registered` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(3) the costs and charges are recoverable as if they had been certified and the certificate registered` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(3) the costs and charges are recoverable as if they had been certified and the certificate registered` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 126(4) to (7) -- garnishment`

-- 126(4): the Commission suspects a person will owe the debtor money; the debtor is liable under Part I, II or VII.1; notice served personally.
#ASSERT `s 126(4) the Commission may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General on account of the second person's liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(4): the debtor is liable under subsection (7) instead; notice sent by a confirmed delivery service.
#ASSERT `s 126(4) the Commission may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General on account of the second person's liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 126(4): no notice served either way.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(4) the Commission may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General on account of the second person's liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(4): the Commission has neither knowledge nor suspicion.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(4) the Commission may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General on account of the second person's liability` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(4): the second person is liable under neither Part I, II or VII.1 nor subsection (7).
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(4) the Commission may require the first person to pay the money otherwise payable to the second person to the Receiver General on account of the second person's liability` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(5)(a): a requirement already made on an employer applies to a future payment of remuneration until the liability is satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(a) the requirement is applicable to the payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(5)(a): once the liability is satisfied, it no longer applies.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(5)(a) the requirement is applicable to the payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 126(5)(a): a payment that is not a future payment of remuneration.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(5)(a) the requirement is applicable to the payment` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(5)(a): no requirement was made under (4).
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(5)(a) the requirement is applicable to the payment` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(5)(b): the employer pays out of each payment the amount stipulated in the notice.
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(b) the amount the employer must pay to the Receiver General out of the payment of remuneration` TRUE TRUE FALSE 150 EQUALS JUST 150
-- 126(5)(b): where the requirement does not apply the subsection says nothing. NOT COVERED: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 126(5)(b) the amount the employer must pay to the Receiver General out of the payment of remuneration` TRUE TRUE TRUE 150 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 126(6): the receipt discharges the original liability to the extent of the payment.
#ASSERT `s 126(6) the amount of the original liability that the receipt discharges` TRUE 200 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 126(6) the amount of the original liability that the receipt discharges` FALSE 200 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 126(6): of an original liability of 500, a payment of 200 leaves 300; a payment that covers it all leaves nothing.
#ASSERT `s 126(6) the original liability that remains after the discharge` TRUE 200 500 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 126(6) the original liability that remains after the discharge` TRUE 500 500 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 126(6) the original liability that remains after the discharge` FALSE 200 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 126(7): an amount not paid as required is a debt due to Her Majesty: required 400, paid 150, so 250.
#ASSERT `s 126(7) the amount not paid as required, which is a debt due to Her Majesty` 400 150 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 126(7) the amount not paid as required, which is a debt due to Her Majesty` 400 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 126(7) the amount not paid as required, which is a debt due to Her Majesty` 400 0 EQUALS 400

§ `s 126(8) and (9) -- service on a business name or a partnership`

-- 126(8): a notice may be addressed to the name or style under which a person carries on business.
#ASSERT `s 126(8) a notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to the name or style under which the person carries on business` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(8) a notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to the name or style under which the person carries on business` FALSE
-- 126(8): personal service is valid if the notice is left with an adult employed at the place of business of the addressee.
#ASSERT `s 126(8) the notice is validly served` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(8) the notice is validly served` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(8) the notice is validly served` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(8) the notice is validly served` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 126(9): a partnership name.
#ASSERT `s 126(9) a notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to a partnership name` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(9) a notice mentioned in subsection (4) may be addressed to a partnership name` FALSE
-- 126(9): personal service on one of the partners, or on an adult employed at the partnership's place of business.
#ASSERT `s 126(9) the notice is validly served` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(9) the notice is validly served` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(9) the notice is validly served` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(9) the notice is validly served` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `s 126(10) to (13) -- inspections`

-- 126(10): an authorized person, at a reasonable time, for the Act's purposes, inspects a document relating to the records.
#ASSERT `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(10): a document relating to the amount of benefits payable is enough on its own.
#ASSERT `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 126(10): not an authorized person; or not at a reasonable time; or not for the Act's purposes; or a document related to neither.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10) an authorized person may inspect or examine the document` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(11): a dwelling-house may be entered only with the occupant's consent or under a warrant.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(11) subsection (11) permits the authorized person to enter the premises or place` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(11) subsection (11) permits the authorized person to enter the premises or place` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(11) subsection (11) permits the authorized person to enter the premises or place` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 126(11): a place that is not a dwelling-house is not caught by the limit.
#ASSERT `s 126(11) subsection (11) permits the authorized person to enter the premises or place` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(10)(a) with (11): a business premises where the authorized person believes records are kept: entry without consent or warrant.
#ASSERT `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(10)(a): belief that persons are or were employed there is enough.
#ASSERT `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(10)(a): the same belief, but the place is a dwelling-house and there is neither consent nor warrant: no entry.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(10)(a): a dwelling-house with the occupant's consent, or under a warrant.
#ASSERT `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 126(10)(a): no belief on reasonable grounds on either point.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(10)(a): not an authorized person.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10)(a) an authorized person may enter the premises or place` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(10)(b): the person in charge must give reasonable assistance and answer proper questions.
#ASSERT `s 126(10)(b) the owner, occupant or person in charge must give the assistance or answer the question` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10)(b) the owner, occupant or person in charge must give the assistance or answer the question` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10)(b) the owner, occupant or person in charge must give the assistance or answer the question` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(10)(b) the owner, occupant or person in charge must give the assistance or answer the question` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(12): a warrant, on the Commission's ex parte application, when the judge is satisfied on all three limbs (cumulative: "and").
#ASSERT `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(12) the judge may issue a warrant authorizing an authorized person to enter the dwelling-house subject to such conditions as may be specified in the warrant` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 126(13): if the judge is not satisfied that entry is necessary, but access has been or may be refused and the document is in the house.
#ASSERT `s 126(13) the judge may order the occupant to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to the document and make such other order as is appropriate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(13) the judge may order the occupant to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to the document and make such other order as is appropriate` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(13) the judge may order the occupant to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to the document and make such other order as is appropriate` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(13) the judge may order the occupant to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to the document and make such other order as is appropriate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(13) the judge may order the occupant to provide an authorized person with reasonable access to the document and make such other order as is appropriate` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

§ `s 126(14) to (20) -- requirements to provide documents and information`

-- 126(15): a requirement on a third party about unnamed persons, without a judge's authorization first obtained: barred.
#ASSERT `s 126(15) the Commission shall not impose the requirement on the third party` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(15): with authorization, no bar; about named persons, no bar; on a person who is not a third party, no bar.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(15) the Commission shall not impose the requirement on the third party` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(15) the Commission shall not impose the requirement on the third party` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(15) the Commission shall not impose the requirement on the third party` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(14): by notice served personally, for the Act's purposes, stating a reasonable time, for information; not barred.
#ASSERT `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(14): by confirmed delivery service, for a document.
#ASSERT `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(14): subject to (15): the same requirement is not allowed where (15) bars it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 126(14): no notice served by either route; no reasonable time stated; neither information nor document; not for the Act's purposes.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(14) the Commission may require the person to provide the information or document` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(16): the judge may authorize on the ex parte application when satisfied on both limbs (a) and (b).
#ASSERT `s 126(16) the judge may authorize the Commission to impose on a third party a requirement relating to an unnamed person or group` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(16) the judge may authorize the Commission to impose on a third party a requirement relating to an unnamed person or group` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(16) the judge may authorize the Commission to impose on a third party a requirement relating to an unnamed person or group` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(16) the judge may authorize the Commission to impose on a third party a requirement relating to an unnamed person or group` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 126(17): a granted authorization must be served together with the notice.
#ASSERT `s 126(17) the authorization must be served together with the notice mentioned in subsection (14)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(17) the authorization must be served together with the notice mentioned in subsection (14)` FALSE
-- 126(18): served on 1 June 2026, the 15 days end on 16 June.
#ASSERT `s 126(18) the last day on which the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 16
#ASSERT `s 126(18) the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 16)
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(18) the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 17)
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(18) the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 2)
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(18) the third party may apply for a review of the authorization` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 2)
-- 126(19): the judge may cancel if not satisfied the (16)(a) and (b) conditions are met, and confirm or vary if satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 126(19) what the judge may do on hearing the application for review` TRUE EQUALS `s 126(19) the judge may confirm or vary the authorization`
#ASSERT `s 126(19) what the judge may do on hearing the application for review` FALSE EQUALS `s 126(19) the judge may cancel the authorization`
-- 126(20)(a): copies of a document inspected, examined or provided may be made by the person or another person acting for the Commission.
#ASSERT `s 126(20)(a) the person may make one or more copies, or have them made` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(20)(a) the person may make one or more copies, or have them made` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(20)(a) the person may make one or more copies, or have them made` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(20)(a) the person may make one or more copies, or have them made` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- 126(20)(b): a copy that appears to be certified is evidence of the nature and content of the original.
#ASSERT `s 126(20)(b) the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document with the same probative force as the original` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(20)(b) the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document with the same probative force as the original` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(20)(b) the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document with the same probative force as the original` FALSE TRUE

§ `s 126(21) and (22) -- compliance, and definitions`

-- 126(21): hindering, preventing, or failing to do what is required unless unable.
#ASSERT `s 126(21) the person contravenes the duty of compliance` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(21) the person contravenes the duty of compliance` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(21) the person contravenes the duty of compliance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 126(21): "unless unable to do so": a person who fails because they are unable does not contravene it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(21) the person contravenes the duty of compliance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(21) the person contravenes the duty of compliance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 126(22): "authorized person": authorized in writing by the Commission for the purposes of the section.
#ASSERT `s 126(22) authorized person` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(22) authorized person` FALSE
-- 126(22): "judge": a superior court judge in the province where the matter arises, or a judge of the Federal Court.
#ASSERT `s 126(22) judge` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 126(22) judge` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(22) judge` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 126(22) judge` FALSE TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 127 and 128 -- repealed`

#EVAL `ss 127 and 128 repealed, and therefore not encoded`
